  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "Salma rows at a speed of 6 metres per second in still water. Water is flowing downstream at a constant speed of $s$ metres per second. Salma rows downstream 140 metres and then returns upstream. Her return journey takes 8 seconds longer. Find $s$, the speed of the water.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$s=1\\text{ m/s}$.\n\nSubtract the downstream time from the upstream time, clear denominators and reject the negative speed.",
      "worked": "The downstream speed is $6+s$ m/s and the upstream speed is $6-s$ m/s, so $0<s<6$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{140}{6-s}-\\frac{140}{6+s}&=8\\\\140(6+s)-140(6-s)&=8(6-s)(6+s)\\\\280s&=8(36-s^2)\\\\35s&=36-s^2\\\\s^2+35s-36&=0\\\\(s+36)(s-1)&=0\\\\s&=-36\\text{ or }1\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $0<s<6$, the water’s speed is $1\\text{ m/s}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
